    <!--
        ⚠ ADDED 2026-09-13 - Read-only object permission on the standard Opportunity object, to fix
        "the Opportunity lookup is not visible when creating an Offering." Offering__c.Opportunity__c
        is a Lookup(Opportunity) field already granted FLS above, but FLS on a lookup field is not
        sufficient by itself: a user also needs at least Read on the lookup's TARGET object, or the
        lookup field renders blank/inaccessible on both the New/Edit form and the detail view even
        though the field itself is on the layout and FLS-granted. Neither this permission set nor
        profiles/DPEG-IR-SF-Minimum Access.profile-meta.xml (src/app) carried any Opportunity object
        permission before this change (confirmed by searching both files for "Opportunity" and
        finding zero objectPermissions grants) - that is the actual root cause of the reported
        symptom, alongside the field's earlier absence from the page layout (fixed separately,
        already applied). SCOPED TO READ ONLY, DELIBERATELY: allowCreate, allowEdit and allowDelete
        are all false, and viewAllRecords/modifyAllRecords are both false. This persona looks up an
        EXISTING Opportunity to link it to an Offering; it does not create, edit, delete, or see
        Opportunities beyond whatever sharing (role hierarchy / sharing rules) already grants it.
        Opportunity is a standard object extended by src/core; granting Read here from an IR-scoped
        permission set does not move or duplicate ownership of the object, it only extends this
        persona's reach to it - the intended way one module's permission set reaches an object it
        does not own (module-boundaries-rule.md).
    -->
    <objectPermissions>
        <allowCreate>false</allowCreate>
        <allowDelete>false</allowDelete>
        <allowEdit>false</allowEdit>
        <allowRead>true</allowRead>
        <modifyAllRecords>false</modifyAllRecords>
        <object>Opportunity</object>
        <viewAllRecords>false</viewAllRecords>
    </objectPermissions>
